
# UNIT III – POLICY OPTIMIZATION

## Adaptive Maze Adventure Game – Intelligent Game Agent Using Policy-Based Reinforcement Learning

### Project Overview

This project focuses on designing, implementing and evaluating an intelligent game agent using Policy-Based Reinforcement Learning techniques.

The project develops an Adaptive Maze Adventure Game in which an autonomous game character navigates through a dynamic maze, collects treasures, avoids enemies, overcomes obstacles and reaches the exit while maximizing rewards.

### Course Information

| Details | Description |
|---|---|
| Unit | Unit III – Policy Optimization |
| Subject | Reinforcement Learning |
| Assignment Theme | Game Development |
| Project | Adaptive Maze Adventure Game |
| Mode | Pair Work – 2 Students |
| Duration | 1 Week |
| Total Marks | 50 |
| Bloom's Levels | K4 – Analyse, K5 – Evaluate |

### Syllabus Covered

- Introduction to Policy-Based Methods
- Vanilla Policy Gradient
- REINFORCE Algorithm
- Stochastic Policy Search
- Actor-Critic Methods
- Advantage Actor-Critic (A2C)
- Asynchronous Advantage Actor-Critic (A3C)
- Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO)
- Trust Region Policy Optimization (TRPO)
- Deep Deterministic Policy Gradient (DDPG)

### Project Objectives

1. Design a dynamic maze environment using Python.
2. Develop an intelligent game agent using policy-based reinforcement learning.
3. Implement stochastic policies for intelligent action selection.
4. Apply policy gradient methods to optimize game strategies.
5. Implement REINFORCE and Actor-Critic algorithms.
6. Analyse and compare A2C and A3C learning mechanisms.
7. Evaluate PPO and TRPO for stable policy optimization.
8. Implement DDPG for continuous action control.
9. Evaluate agent performance using rewards, game completion rates and training results.

### Problem Statement

The game character must navigate through a maze containing walls, empty paths, treasures, moving enemies and an exit point.

The agent can perform four basic actions:

- Up
- Down
- Left
- Right

The environment provides positive rewards for collecting treasures and reaching the exit, while negative rewards are given for hitting obstacles and encountering enemies.

The main objective is to train an intelligent agent that learns an effective action-selection strategy and successfully completes the game under changing environmental conditions.

### Assignment Tasks

#### Q1 – Design and Analyse the Adaptive Maze Adventure Game Environment (8 Marks)

- Design a maze environment of at least 5 × 5 cells.
- Define state space, action space, reward function and terminal conditions.
- Identify the game character, enemies, obstacles, treasures and exit.
- Implement different maze configurations.
- Analyse stochastic policies and reward-based decision-making.
- Compare rule-based and policy-based game agents.

#### Q2 – Implement Vanilla Policy Gradient and REINFORCE (10 Marks)

- Develop a stochastic policy for action selection.
- Implement the REINFORCE algorithm.
- Calculate discounted returns using a discount factor.
- Update policy parameters using policy gradients.
- Train the agent for at least 100 episodes.
- Analyse training rewards and game completion rates.

#### Q3 – Design and Implement Actor-Critic Algorithms (10 Marks)

- Design Actor and Critic networks.
- Implement state-value estimation.
- Calculate temporal-difference error and advantage.
- Investigate A2C and A3C algorithms.
- Compare REINFORCE and Actor-Critic methods.
- Evaluate training stability and convergence behaviour.

#### Q4 – Analyse and Compare PPO and TRPO (10 Marks)

- Implement Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO).
- Study the clipped objective function.
- Understand probability ratios and clipping parameters.
- Analyse Trust Region Policy Optimization (TRPO).
- Compare PPO and TRPO in terms of stability and computational requirements.
- Evaluate performance under changing obstacle configurations.

#### Q5 – Develop and Evaluate an Intelligent Game Agent Using DDPG (12 Marks)

- Design a 2D continuous-control game environment.
- Implement Actor and Critic networks.
- Develop a DDPG agent.
- Apply experience replay and target networks.
- Implement soft target network updates.
- Compare DDPG with PPO or A2C.
- Evaluate performance using cumulative rewards, completion rates and training stability.

### Algorithms Used

| Algorithm | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Vanilla Policy Gradient | Policy optimization |
| REINFORCE | Episode-based policy learning |
| A2C | Synchronous Actor-Critic learning |
| A3C | Asynchronous Actor-Critic learning |
| PPO | Stable policy optimization |
| TRPO | Constrained policy updates |
| DDPG | Continuous action control |

### Technologies Used

- Programming Language: Python
- Libraries: NumPy, Matplotlib
- Deep Learning Frameworks: TensorFlow / Keras or PyTorch
- Game Development: Pygame
- Reinforcement Learning Environment: Gymnasium
- Version Control: Git and GitHub

### Experimental Evaluation

The game agent is evaluated using the following performance measures:

- Total episode reward.
- Number of steps taken.
- Number of treasures collected.
- Number of enemy collisions.
- Game completion rate.
- Survival time.
- Training stability and convergence.

### Expected Results

- Successful navigation through different maze configurations.
- Intelligent treasure collection and enemy avoidance.
- Improved action selection through policy optimization.
- Stable learning through Actor-Critic methods.
- Improved policy updates using PPO and TRPO.
- Continuous movement control using DDPG.
- Performance comparisons through reward graphs and experimental observations.

### Pair Work and Responsibilities

Both students participate in all five questions and individually execute the required programs in their respective GitHub repositories.

The assignment follows the learning process:

**Design → Implementation → Analysis → Evaluation**

Student A and Student B alternate individual responsibilities across the questions while jointly understanding and defending the complete assignment.

### Conclusion

This project demonstrates the application of policy-based reinforcement learning algorithms in intelligent game development.

By implementing and evaluating Vanilla Policy Gradient, REINFORCE, Actor-Critic, PPO, TRPO and DDPG, the project explores how autonomous game agents can learn effective strategies in dynamic environments.

The ultimate goal is to develop an adaptive intelligent game agent capable of making effective decisions, maximizing rewards and successfully navigating changing game conditions.

